      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><h1 id=\"loading-a-raw-ufo-model\">Loading a raw UFO model</h1>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">This tutorial crosses FeynKit's optional UFO boundary: a conventional Python UFO package is normalized into the same typed <code>Model</code> used by the core diagram and expression APIs. We use a tiny scalar theory so every diagnostic count is easy to inspect.</span></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
    {
      "id": "vblA",
      "code_hash": "fd529f23286ed93cd77a3d9bc5634a51",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><h2 id=\"requirements\">Requirements</h2>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">Raw UFO import requires <strong>Python 3.11 or newer</strong> and <code>ufo-model-loader&gt;=0.1.6</code>. Install the supported extra with:</span>\n<div class=\"language-bash codehilite\"><pre><span></span><code>pip<span class=\"w\"> </span>install<span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s1\">'symbolica[feynkit-ufo]'</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">This is an explicit optional workflow. The normalized JSON tutorials <code>00</code>\u2013<code>03</code> need only the base <code>symbolica</code> package.</span></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
    {
      "id": "bkHC",
      "code_hash": "34102233cba0543ab7f8634234ec4052",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/plain": ""
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
    {
      "id": "lEQa",
      "code_hash": "41f9765898ae4589ce34884286da31fd",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><h2 id=\"normalize-the-ufo-package\">Normalize the UFO package</h2>\n<span class=\"paragraph\"><code>UfoLoader.load</code> returns three typed results together: <code>model</code> for physics operations, <code>parameters</code> for the applied numerical inputs, and <code>diagnostics</code> recording exactly how normalization was requested. <code>restriction_name=\"default\"</code> applies <code>restrict_default.dat</code>.</span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">The environment variable below belongs to this teaching fixture\u2014not to FeynKit generally. It limits this generated scalar model to two- and three-point interactions, keeping the tutorial fast and deterministic.</span></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
    {
      "id": "PKri",
      "code_hash": "c4ae4bdb7e2c07c1b33f79175ac9b0b9",
      "outputs": [
